      "id": "prop-a-finite-simplicial-complex-has-compact-hausdorff-realization",
      "concern": "Step 2.2 says that arbitrary ambient-open extensions O_σ of U∩|σ| imply U=(∪_σ O_σ)∩|K|. This equality need not follow: an extension chosen for one simplex can contain points of another simplex outside U. The compact-Hausdorff claim is true, but Hausdorffness needs a valid finite gluing/subspace-topology argument.",
