    {
      "id": "cor-adapted-classes-compute-derived-functors",
      "concern": "In step 1.1 (and dually 1.2), the proof says the newly defined cokernel/kernel is “still in D.” The stated closure of C applies only to cokernels of monomorphisms between objects of C (dually kernels of epimorphisms between objects of C), while Z^q is only known to lie in D. The displayed construction separately writes Z^{q+1}∈D, but the proof treats this as a consequence without a closure hypothesis on D or a choice of maps whose cokernels/kernels remain in D.",
